{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["בן פורת יוסף בן פורת עלי עין — this verse is like interlaced half-lines at the beginning of a verse; rather, he mentions about whom he is speaking and then repeats and doubles the first half-line and completes his utterance, as in: ״נשאו נהרות ה׳ נשאו נהרות קולם״. ״כי הנה אויביך ה׳ כי הנה אויביך יאבדו״. ״עד מתי רשעים ה׳ עד מתי רשעים יעלוזו״. ״הבל הבלים אמר קהלת הבל הבלים הכל הבל״. ״ימינך ה׳ נאדרי בכח ימינך ה׳ תרעץ אויב״." "So too here: בן פורת יוסף — a son of a fruitful one, and Yoseif grew. And upon what did he grow?" "בן פורת עלי עין — he grew and multiplied above the eye, to look down from above the eye, in his stature and in his beauty. The daughters of Egypt." "צעדה — each and every one." "עלי שור — a term of seeing. It doubles the expression of עלי עין. As in: ״ומגבעות אשורנו״ — that the daughters of Egypt would step and walk to see him, like the wife of Potifar and her companions. And from this —"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:53.182937344Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}